schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Recommendation: hold 2-3 years of operating expenses in stablecoins"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "The most practical solution: maintain 2-3 years of operating expenses
    in stablecoins like USDC or DAI" as a DAO treasury's survival buffer
    through bear markets.
  evidence: >-
    Argued from the four stated benefits (resilience during downturns,
    predictable budgeting, contributor flexibility, yield/credit
    opportunities) — no external study, dataset, or named DAO case is cited
    to support the specific "2-3 years" figure.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/treasury-management.md
  interpretation: >-
    This is a concrete financial/governance recommendation a reader could
    act on directly (how much of a DAO's treasury to hold, and in what
    form) — the kind of guidance that materially affects a DAO's finances
    and decision-making power if followed uncritically.
  uncertainty: >-
    The "2-3 years" figure is presented as a rule of thumb without
    supporting data or named precedent; appropriate runway depends heavily
    on a specific DAO's burn rate, revenue, and risk tolerance.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/treasury-management.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
